return nft_parse_register_store(ctx, tb[NFTA_EXTHDR_DREG], &priv->dreg, NULL, NFT_DATA_VALUE, priv->len);
Reason:
When `NFT_EXTHDR_F_PRESENT` is set, the evaluation path writes only 1 byte (via `nft_reg_store8`) or 4 bytes (zero on error), but `nft_parse_register_store()` marks `priv->len` (user-controlled) bytes as initialized in the register bitmap. If `len > 4`, registers beyond the first are considered initialized while still containing uninitialized stack data, causing information disclosure.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if ((flags & NFT_EXTHDR_F_PRESENT) && len != 1)
	return -EINVAL;
Reason:
This check ensures that when the `F_PRESENT` flag is used, the requested length must be exactly 1 byte—the only actual data written by the evaluation path. This prevents the register tracking mismatch by rejecting invalid configurations where `len > 1`.

